# Java Spring Services

## Stack (pinned — see docs/tech-stack.md)

- **JDK 21 LTS**, **Spring Boot 4.1.x** (start 4.1.1)
- **Spring Cloud 2025.1.x** for Gateway (`api-gateway`)
- Spring Security (JWT), Data JPA, Kafka, Redis — versions from Boot BOM
- Build: **Gradle 8.14+** with Wrapper (`build.gradle`, Groovy DSL)
- Migrations: **Flyway** (`V{n}__description.sql`)
- Tests: JUnit 5, Mockito, Spring Boot Test

## Layout (per service under `java-services/{name}/`)

```
src/main/java/.../{api,application,domain,infrastructure}
src/main/resources/application.yml
src/main/resources/db/migration/
build.gradle
settings.gradle
gradlew / gradlew.bat
gradle/wrapper/
```

## API

- REST under `/api/v1/...` (routes in `docs/services-mvp.md`)
- Validate at DTO boundary; clear error bodies
- OpenAPI via springdoc when the service is wired

## Data & events

- JPA entities map to tables this service owns (`docs/database.md`)
- Publish Kafka events **after** successful DB commit
- Redis for sessions/permissions cache per tech-stack + microservice docs

## Do

```java
// ✅ Persist first, then publish
taskRepository.save(task);
kafkaTemplate.send("task.assigned", event);
```

## Don't

```java
// ❌ Publish before persistence succeeds
kafkaTemplate.send("task.assigned", event);
taskRepository.save(task);
```

- Do not target Boot 3.5 (OSS EOL) or switch Java services to Maven — Gradle is the project standard
